prompt:
Something about the type on our recipe blog feels off. It's cramped and kind of cheap-looking but I can't say why. Here's the CSS, can you tell me what's wrong and what to change?

body {
  font-family: Georgia, serif;
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.15;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  text-align: justify;
  color: #333;
}
.post { width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; }
h1 { font-size: 56px; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 700; }
h2.tag { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0; font-weight: 400; }
a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
a:hover { color: #c0392b; }
.price, .qty { font-family: Georgia, serif; }
blockquote { font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; }

This is the stylesheet for the tenant-rights guide on our legal aid clinic's site. It's about to go live and I just want a last typography pass from you before I hand it off. Fix whatever needs fixing.

:root { --ink: #1d2327; --muted: #5a646b; --link: #0b5cab; }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
body {
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.125rem;
  line-height: 1.6;
  color: var(--ink);
  margin: 0;
}
main { max-width: 38rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.015em; margin: 0 0 1rem; text-wrap: balance; }
h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; text-wrap: balance; }
p { margin: 0 0 1em; hyphens: auto; }
p + p { margin-top: 0; }
a { color: var(--link); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.15em; text-decoration-thickness: 0.08em; }
a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 2px; }
small, .note { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); }
.label { font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; font-weight: 600; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
td, th { padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; text-align: left; }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; }
code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; }
